  "raw": " MPs \"could have refined\" their debate.\n\nDuring a press conference yesterday at Parliament, DA Secretary-General factional heads Lewis Nzimande and Bonginkosi Madikizela also avoided any mention of Opposition Leader Mmusi Maimane who is on an extended leave in London battling split eardrums.\n\nNzimande said his party supported the bill as it improved the lives of black people. But he received little sympathy from commentators questioning why \"outgoing Labour Minister Mildred Oliphant\" missed out on the attention for her own contribution to business and education.\n\nIn what appeared to be partly a diversion tactic, Nzimanda defended Elections Strategic Communications Director Kagiso Motha against claims that EFF leader Julius Malema had dodged a journalist's questions today by telling them to go to a cabinet announcement to find such things out as Motha accused Amathole Constituency Councillor Ntuthuko Maseko personally attacking",
  "serialized": "MPs \"could have refined\" their debate. During a press conference yesterday at Parliament, DA Secretary-General factional heads Lewis Nzimande and Bonginkosi Madikizela also avoided any mention of Opposition Leader Mmusi Maimane who is on an extended leave in London battling split eardrums. Nzimande said his party supported the bill as it improved the lives of black people. But he received little sympathy from commentators questioning why \"outgoing Labour Minister Mildred Oliphant\" missed out on the attention for her own contribution to business and education. In what appeared to be partly a diversion tactic, Nzimanda defended Elections Strategic Communications Director Kagiso Motha against claims that EFF leader Julius Malema had dodged a journalist's questions today by telling them to go to a cabinet announcement to find such things out as Motha accused Amathole Constituency Councillor Ntuthuko Maseko personally attacking",
